The '''2000 United States Senate election in Texas''' took place on November 7, 2000. Republican incumbent [[Kay Bailey Hutchison]] won re-election to a second full term in a landslide over Gene Kelly. 

{{As of|2026}}, this election and the [[2000 United States presidential election in Texas|concurrent United States presidential election]] were the last time [[Travis County, Texas|Travis County]] voted Republican in any statewide election and the last time any candidate won every county in the [[Texas Triangle]] in a statewide election.

